{
  "_source": "The next question the assistant may offer after an answer — build-plan row 11d, docs/assistant.md §13 (D-65). Cowork 10.11.2026. `buttons`: id → the label in the customer's own voice (NL u-form / RO tu-form; these labels are the strings, there is no second copy in the lexicon) and what a tap does: entry = that answer of assistant-faq.json · pick = the order helper's pick · cards = the „Past erbij” / „Merge cu” cards of §13.4 (assistant-pairings.json first, then the four data sources) · say = a lexicon §5.37 line built from the data. needs = what must be true for the button to exist at all. until = the last day it may be shown. `after`: the first row whose `when` fits the answer just given decides; `offer` is an ordered list of candidates and the box shows the first two that pass `rules` — often one, sometimes none. `product` on a row = the product the buttons refer to when the answer names none. stage = §13.3's five places (looking · weighing · planning · ordering · practical), kept for the weekly count only. Checked 10.11 16:3x against the engine itself (built from src with this folder's bank): every `entry` exists, none is a hand-off-only or an allergen answer; a typed sentence was dropped as a tap's action because the engine read „Cum se gătește Mici?” as „do you have mici” — a tap goes straight to its answer.",
  "rules": {
    "max": 2,
    "where": "under the answer, after it is complete (after the last streamed word); never before or instead of the answer",
    "a_tap": "is a known question: answered by the local engine at once, no model call, also when the layer is on; the customer's bubble shows the label; the turn is added to the history the layer receives with the next typed message; one numbers-only log row (model_called false, tapped = [id])",
    "passed": "never a button whose answer the conversation already holds (its entry / say / cards were already given, typed or tapped) and never the button for the question just asked",
    "not_twice": "a button shown twice in this conversation and not tapped is not shown a third time",
    "needs": {
      "product": "a product is known: named in the answer, the row's `product`, the open product sheet, or state.last",
      "pairing": "assistant-pairings.json has a row for it, or one of the four data sources of §13.4 gives at least one card other than the product itself",
      "product.line": "the product has a cooking line",
      "product.in-colli": "at least one colli's contents name it",
      "product.is-colli": "the product is a colli",
      "product.kg-meat": "sold per kg and in one of: rund, varken, kip, lam, marinades, roemeens — the discount's own scope (FACTS: only meat, only on order)",
      "no-card-with-add": "the answer does not already show that product's card with its own add button",
      "no-recipe-link": "the answer does not already carry the „Recept →” link of that product",
      "no-colli-link": "the answer does not already carry a link to a colli that holds it",
      "contents-not-said": "the answer did not already give the colli's contents"
    },
    "never": {
      "topics": [
        "allergens",
        "legal"
      ],
      "entries_handoff_always": [
        "allergen-serious",
        "legal-complaint",
        "products-fresh-frozen",
        "products-voucher",
        "traiteur-bbq-home"
      ],
      "intents": [
        "allergen",
        "miss-1",
        "miss-2",
        "handoff",
        "person",
        "scope",
        "complaint",
        "clarify"
      ],
      "also": "a reply that carries the order helper's own chips or its handover buttons (the helper leads); an answer that shows an offer row (one nudge at a time); the bubble of the salute and the greeting"
    },
    "layer_on": "the model does not write chips any more: `present.chips` becomes a list of at most two ids of `buttons`; the server keeps only ids that pass these rules, fills {product} and draws the labels of this file. No ids from the model = no buttons. The `after` table is used by the local engine alone (layer off, fallback, taps).",
    "counts": "every answer logs the ids it showed (`shown`); every tap logs one row (`tapped` = [id]); a handover row („Naar de bestelbon” / „Via WhatsApp”) carries all ids tapped so far in this conversation (`tapped`); the first turn of a conversation is flagged (`first`). docs/sql/qa-asks-11d.sql.",
    "say": {
      "cookLine": "the product's own cooking line of products.json, word for word",
      "colliContents": "the colli's own line of products.json (weight and contents) and its price",
      "inColli": "lexicon §5.37 „{product} zit in {list}.”, {list} from the colli lines that name the product",
      "askTown": "lexicon §5.37 „In welke gemeente woont u? …”; the next message is read as a town or postcode (the delivery-by-town answer of row 11b)"
    }
  },
